{
 "_doc": "Stream C (play-test 5: T3 direct heals, T4 revives). What Thousandvale changes in Farhold's skill table, applied IN MEMORY at engine boot by js/rules/tv-skills.js (Farhold's data/skills.json is shared with a live game and is never written). `patch`: fields merged onto an existing row (a `forms` entry is merged per form; null removes a field). `add`: whole new rows, each with its own talent tree in Farhold's format (4 tiers x 2 nodes, every node a rule \u2014 never a plain number). `classes`: the six skill ids of a class, by key 1-6. A row's `tv` block holds what only Thousandvale's rules read (js/rules/cast-skills.js): `tv.revive` = { share (health the body returns with, 0..1), mp (mana share, optional), castTime (seconds, 0 = instant), combat (may it be cast while a monster attacks you), mass (every fallen party member in range, else one), range (m), style (the look D-world draws), apply: { status: {id, seconds?}, barrier: {share, seconds}, debuff: {id, name, seconds, dealLess, takeMore} } }. The card sentences for a `tv` block are written from these numbers by js/rules/wording.js. The parity fixtures build their engine with tvSkills off (tests/C/setup.mjs). `tv.touch` = a touch heal's reach in metres (a party member further than that is not reached: it lands on the caster).",
